Subject: [PATCH 3/6] phyFLEX-stm32mp2 M33 I2C Temp Sensor example:
 stm32cubemp2 v1.3.2

   The default I2C_TwoBoards_ComPolling example has the following behavior:

   - uses I2C8 to communicate between two STM32MP257-EV1 boards.
   - configures one board as master and the other as slave.
   - waits for a USER2 button press before the master sends a predefined message.
   - waits for another button press before the master receives a message back.
   - compares the transmitted and received buffers, then blinks LED3 on success.

   Here we are changing the example to read a P3T1755 temperature sensor located
   on the phyFLEX-STM32MP257 Development Kit Carrier Board using I2C1 and print
   the temperature over UART5 every three seconds (without flow control! access
   at reference designator JP1):

   - uses PI1 for I2C1 SDA and PG13 for I2C1 SCL.
   - uses the sensor's 7-bit address 0x4F, with A0, A1 and A2 pulled high.
   - reads two bytes from temperature register 0x00 using blocking HAL calls.
   - converts the signed 12-bit reading to degrees Celsius.
   - prints through UART5 on PG9 (TX), configured for 115200 baud, 8N1.
   - toggles LED3 after a successful reading and prints a message on read failure.
   - runs automatically without waiting for a button press.

   Linux I2C1 must be disabled in the active device tree so it does not compete
   with the Cortex-M33 for the peripheral. The updated M33-examples overlay
   must be compiled, deployed to /boot/overlays/, and enabled at boot.

Signed-off-by: True Loan <tloan@phytec.com>
